{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the process. I need to:\n\n1. Create build scripts under `.xorq/scripts/` for both datasets\n2. Build them and add to the catalog\n3. Create a derived metric script that reads both sources and calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Query and verify the result\n\nLet me start by creating the scripts directory and the build scripts.\n\nFor the farmers markets data, I need to:\n- Read the CSV from the URL\n- Filter out territories (to get only states)\n- Sum up the farmers markets\n\nFor the population data:\n- Read the CSV from the URL\n- Get the 2025 population for the \"United States\" row\n\nFor the metric:\n- Read both and calculate: (total farmers markets / total population) * 100,000\n\nLet me start with building scripts for the raw data ingestion.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll ingest both datasets and create the metric. Let me start by setting up the scripts directory and creating build scripts for both data sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ByYVgKosMAcv4g3msHCQmt","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts .xorq/builds"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":295,"cacheRead":8743,"cacheWrite":4744,"totalTokens":13795,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0014750000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0008743000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00593,"total":0.0082923},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":195},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912433844,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74mRnkjHfaHrkim7UJL","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
